From 2b2d1e997e8061b63aa771babfe69479a54f2229 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mesh-LLM CI <ci@mesh-llm.local>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 09:20:42 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 30/32] test(skippy): cover head-input publication and stage
 capture

DeepSeek-V4 publishes the head input as the mean of its hyper-connection
streams, so the final stage of a split must keep it: its stage capture
covers target layers 41, 42 and 43 on every stage of an even 2- and
4-way cut, and llama_layer_inp_published reports it. Its verify-rollback
case runs in native-rollback mode.
---
 src/CMakeLists.txt                          |  16 +++
 src/skippy/tests/graph_build_inputs.cpp     | 112 +++++++++++++++++---
 src/skippy/tests/graph_contract_cases.cmake |  23 ++++
 3 files changed, 134 insertions(+), 17 deletions(-)

